        "messageOrdinal": 80,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-08-16",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "16 August 1845",
        "text": "See how little!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s1931",
        "messageOrdinal": 130,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-10-16",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "16 October 1845",
        "text": "My cage is not worse but better since you brought the green groundsel to it--and to dash oneself against the wires of it will not open the door.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s1995",
        "messageOrdinal": 134,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-10-22",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "22 October 1845",
        "text": "May God bless you.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s7402",
        "messageOrdinal": 368,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-05-22",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "22 May 1846",
        "text": "At that turn of the road they lost the track of the hare.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s7478",
        "messageOrdinal": 372,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-05-25",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "25 May 1846",
        "text": "I blame myself often.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s8456",
        "messageOrdinal": 416,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-06-22",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "22 June 1846",
        "text": "The next news is not so good,—for I have had a note from Mrs. Jameson to the effect that she will come to take me to the pictures to-morrow, Monday—so that there will be no time to be diplomatic.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s9666",
        "messageOrdinal": 467,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-07-22",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "22 July 1846",
        "text": "Will you do so, because you were loved in them as a beginning, or because you were free? (Am I not as bad as Flush, to ask such questions?)",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s12383",
        "messageOrdinal": 564,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-09-16",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "16 September 1846",
        "text": "I thank God, as you do, and see his hand in it.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      }
    ]
  }
